">ע\"ג</span>) as though (carried) on &c.; a. v. fr.—<a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Targum_Jonathan_on_Isaiah.29.15\" data-ref=\"Targum Jonathan on Isaiah 29:15\">Targ. Is. XXIX, 15</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">כִּדְבְּקִבְלָא</span> (ed. Lag. <span dir=\"rtl\">כיד בק׳</span>) as though in darkness. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Onkelos_Numbers.29.18\" data-ref=\"Onkelos Numbers 29:18\">Targ. O. Num. XXIX, 18</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">כדחזי</span>, v. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_חֲזִי.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, חֲזִי 1\">חֲזִי</a>, as it is proper; a. fr.—<a class=\"refLink\" href=\"Jerusalem_Talmud_Avodah_Zarah.3.1.5\" data-ref=\"Jerusalem Talmud Avodah Zarah 3:1:5\">Y. Ab. Zar. III, 42ᶜ</a> top. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"Jerusalem_Talmud_Yoma.7.1.5\" data-ref=\"Jerusalem Talmud Yoma 7:1:5\">Y. Yoma VII, 44ᵇ</a> top <span dir=\"rtl\">כד דהיא וכ׳</span> when there is &c. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"Jerusalem_Talmud_Taanit.1.2.4\" data-ref=\"Jerusalem Talmud Taanit 1:2:4\">Y. Taan. I, 64ᵃ</a> bot. <span dir=\"rtl\">כד הוינן</span>; Y. Meg. III, 74ᵇ bot. <span dir=\"rtl\">כרי דהוינן</span>, v. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_נְהַר I.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, נְהַר I 1\"><span dir=\"rtl\">נְהַר</span> I</a>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Bava_Kamma.52a.5\" data-ref=\"Bava Kamma 52a:5\">B. Kam. 52ᵃ</a> (prov.) <span dir=\"rtl\">כד רגיז וכ׳</span> when the shepherd is angry with his flock, he makes a blind sheep the leader. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Bava_Kamma.64b\" data-ref=\"Bava Kamma 64b\">Ib. 64ᵇ</a>, a. fr. <span dir=\"rtl\">כִּדְּאַמְרֵי וכ׳</span> as they say &c. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Bava_Kamma.64b.7\" data-ref=\"Bava Kamma 64b:7\">Ib. 64ᵇ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">כִּדְּתָנָא דבי וכ׳</span> as (that which) the scholars of the school of … said. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Bava_Kamma.64b.21\" data-ref=\"Bava Kamma 64b:21\">Ib.</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">מיבעי ליה לכִדְּתָנִי</span> it is needed for (something like) what has been taught. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Bava_Kamma.64b.11\" data-ref=\"Bava Kamma 64b:11\">Ib.</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">לְכִדְּרָבָא</span> for what Raba said. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Bava_Metzia.99b.8\" data-ref=\"Bava Metzia 99b:8\">B. Mets. 99ᵇ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">כדרבא</span> agreeably to what R. said; a. v. fr.—[<a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Bamidbar_Rabbah.14.22\" data-ref=\"Bamidbar Rabbah 14:22\">Num. R. s. 14</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">א\"ת כדרבונות אלא כִּדֵּרַבָּניּת</span> read not (<a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.12.11\" data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 12:11\">Koh. XII, 11</a>) <i>kaddarbonoth</i>, but <i>kidd’rabbanuth</i>, like a command of authority.]"}]}, "plural_form": [], "alt_headwords": ["כִּיד", "כִּדּ־", "כִּידּ־"], "quotes": [], "prev_hw": "כגני", "next_hw": "כַּד II", "parent_lexicon_details": {"name": "Jastrow Dictionary", "language": "heb.talmudic", "to_language": "eng", "text_categories": [], "source": "Jastrow Dictionary", "attribution": "Rabbi Marcus Jastrow", "index_title": "Jastrow", "version_title": "London, Luzac, 1903", "version_lang": "en", "should_autocomplete": true}}, {"headword": "כַּד II", "parent_lexicon": "Jastrow Dictionary", "rid": "K00099", "refs": ["Avodah Zarah 40a:8", "Chullin 64a:2", "Chullin 64a:6", "Bamidbar Rabbah 12:1", "Bamidbar Rabbah 12:2", "Bamidbar Rabbah 12:3", "Bamidbar Rabbah 12:4", "Bamidbar Rabbah 12:5", "Bamidbar Rabbah 12:6", "Bamidbar Rabbah 12:7", "Bamidbar Rabbah 12:8", "Bamidbar Rabbah 12:9", "Bamidbar Rabbah 12:10", "Bamidbar Rabbah 12:11", "Bamidbar Rabbah 12:12", "Bamidbar Rabbah 12:13", "Bamidbar Rabbah 12:14", "Bamidbar Rabbah 12:15", "Bamidbar Rabbah 12:16", "Bamidbar Rabbah 12:17", "Bamidbar Rabbah 12:18", "Bamidbar Rabbah 12:19", "Bamidbar Rabbah 12:20", "Bamidbar Rabbah 12:21", "Bereishit Rabbah 61:1", "Bereishit Rabbah 61:2", "Bereishit Rabbah 61:3", "Bereishit Rabbah 61:4", "Bereishit Rabbah 61:5", "Bereishit Rabbah 61:6", "Bereishit Rabbah 61:7", "Midrash Tehillim 1:1", "Midrash Tehillim 1:2", "Midrash Tehilli